-- "Are we in the middle of an auction?", in one place, because several
-- features need the same answer and each one guessing at it separately is how
-- they drift apart. Returns nil when the coast is clear, otherwise the reason
-- in words so the caller can print it. SEARCHING plus a spent settle window is
-- the only moment nothing is riding on the player's position.
function AUCTION.BusyReason()
	if AUCTION.winRunning then
		return "the auto-win sequence is holding position"
	end
	if AUCTION.state ~= "SEARCHING" then
		return "in an auction (" .. tostring(AUCTION.state) .. ")"
	end
	if os.clock() < (AUCTION.settleUntil or 0) then
		return "an auction has just ended and the loot is still landing"
	end
	return nil
end

