-- =========================================================
-- ITEM RULES (UI) -- a summary, a button, and eight hidden save slots.
-- =========================================================
-- What this replaced, and why: the rules used to be eight RayVoid slots of
-- nineteen controls each -- 175 controls on one page. The user's verdict was
-- "way too confusing", and they were right: what they actually wanted to say
-- was "keep a gavel if it looks like ANY of these four things", and a flat
-- list of criteria cannot say "any of" at all.
--
-- So the rule shape changed (see the engine above) and the editor moved into
-- a window we build ourselves, the same Instance.new pattern as the event
-- predictor. RayVoid controls are one-per-setting by construction, which is
-- exactly wrong for a variable-length list of setups.
--
-- STORAGE STAYS RAYVOID. Each rule is a JSON string in a hidden CreateInput
-- whose Flag is Rule<N>Data, so rules are saved and restored by the config
-- slot machinery like every other setting -- which matters, because the user
-- keeps several slots and a bespoke save file would not follow the one they
-- just loaded. The window only reads and writes those flags.
-- Everything already on this page at this point is a per-lane exclusion list
-- (built just above), so it is captured here and collapsed. The toggle that
-- controls it is spared by name -- it has to stay reachable to switch them
-- back on. Same page-diff technique as the hidden save slots below: RayVoid
-- exposes no visibility control on ordinary elements, but the page itself is
-- a ScrollingFrame whose UIListLayout skips invisible children, so a hidden
-- block collapses rather than leaving a gap.
pcall(function()
	local rayfield = game:GetService("CoreGui"):FindFirstChild("RobloxGui")
	rayfield = rayfield and rayfield:FindFirstChild("Rayfield")
	local main = rayfield and rayfield:FindFirstChild("Main")
	local elements = main and main:FindFirstChild("Elements")
	RULES.page = elements and elements:FindFirstChild("Item Rules")
end)

-- Everything the lanes registered is hidden here, once, now that they have
-- all been built. The rule editor window is where they are edited.
FILTERS.HideAll()

